# React Native guide

Act as a top-tier software engineer with extensive React Native ecosystem knowledge to build high-quality cross-platform mobile applications.

## Before Writing Code

- Observe the project's relevant existing code.
- Conform to existing code style, patterns, and conventions unless directed otherwise. Note: these instructions count as "directed otherwise" unless the user explicitly overrides them.

## Principles

- Display/container component pattern
  - Split your component into display components, which are pure functions that map props to JSX, and container components, which are (optional) stateful components that wrap one display component.
  - Then compose them together in the parent or screen/route component.

Constraints {
Be concise.
You're using Expo Router for navigation (file-based routing, same mental model as React Router).
Use Zustand for client/UI state (auth session, onboarding flags, ephemeral UI). Prefer small feature stores in `src/stores/` with kebab-case files (e.g. `app-store.ts`). Select state with selectors: `useAppStore((s) => s.user)` — never subscribe to the whole store by default.
Use TanStack Query (`@tanstack/react-query`) for server/async data (fetching, caching, mutations). Put the `QueryProvider` at the root. Colocate query keys, query fns, and hooks by feature (e.g. `src/features/sessions/use-sessions-query.ts`). Prefer `useQuery` / `useMutation` over manual `useEffect` + `useState` data fetching.
Do not put server cache in Zustand. Do not put ephemeral client UI state in TanStack Query.
Forms: prefer `react-hook-form` for multi-field forms. Wire inputs with `Controller` into existing `@/components` (`Field`, `DateField`, `Chip`, `SegmentedControl`). Keep in-progress form state in the form (or a short-lived Zustand draft for cross-screen pickers) — never in TanStack Query. Submit via feature `use-*-mutation.ts` hooks; surface `ApiError.detail` / `ApiError.fieldErrors` to the UI. Client validation must match the API contract (enums, max lengths, ranges). One- or two-field screens may stay on local `useState`.
Images: pick with `expo-image-picker`, crop/compress with `expo-image-manipulator`, then upload via the feature’s signed-upload flow (do not invent a new media stack).
Dates: pick with `DateField` (`@react-native-community/datetimepicker`). Store/submit ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. Do not use a free-text date input.
Sessions / pitches: colocate under `src/features/sessions/` and `src/features/pitches/` (api, types, query keys, `use-*-query` / `use-*-mutation`). Hold the Start Session wizard in `useStartSessionDraftStore` (`start-session-draft-store.ts`) — not TanStack Query. Play structure is constrained by session type (match forced halves; futsal halves|sets; training forced `training_activities` + activity chips). Extra-time Yes/No + length is a second duration step after planned segment length when structure is halves. Training without `set` skips pitch setup entirely. Location for nearby pitches and End A/B corner marks: `expo-location` via `src/features/pitches/location.ts` (`getCurrentDeviceLocation`). Do not add a map library for pitch marking.
Live GPS tracking (Feature 0.4 / 0.42): colocate under `src/features/sessions/tracking/` — SQLite local store (`db.ts`), background fixes via `expo-location` + `expo-task-manager` (`location-task.ts`), HUD in `useTrackingHudStore` (`tracking-store.ts`), orchestration in `use-tracking-session.ts` and `session-lifecycle.ts`. Capture OS `coords.speedAccuracy` via config plugin `plugins/with-speed-accuracy.js` (patches expo-location iOS/Android serialization; requires a native rebuild — not Expo Go); store as nullable `speed_accuracy_mps` on `tracking_points` and include it on track-points upload (`null` when unavailable). Live HUD top speed uses `determineTopSpeedKmh` in `speed-filter.ts` (F1–F4), not raw max OS speed. Push Live Activity / FGS notification updates from the location task (`indicator.ts` `refreshTrackingIndicator`) so distance and top speed keep moving when the app is backgrounded or the screen is locked. iOS Live Activity via `expo-live-activity`; Android FGS body updates in-place via the local `tracking-indicator` module (do not stop/restart the location task to change the notification). Only call `startLocationUpdatesAsync` while `AppState` is `active` — Android 12+ cannot start a foreground service from the background. Request POST_NOTIFICATIONS on Android 13+. Hold-to-confirm pause/end uses `HoldToConfirmButton`. After half 2, if `extra_time_enabled`, surface ADD EXTRA TIME (segments 3–4) instead of HALF TIME. Training HUD shows the live activity (e.g. RUN 1 · IN PROGRESS) with END RUN/DRILL/SET; that closes the segment into a rest state, then START RUN/DRILL/SET opens the next. End session → local finalize + background sync (`sync.ts`); do not route to session summary (0.5).
Native Android/iOS: `android/` and `ios/` are gitignored (CNG). Do not edit them. Patch generated files with an Expo config plugin under `plugins/` and register it last in `app.config.ts` (e.g. `with-safe-react-delegate` for the RN 0.81 `onUserLeaveHint` NPE; `with-speed-accuracy` for OS speed accuracy on location coords).
Pitch ends (presentation): API/storage use `end_a` / `end_b`. In UI copy and schematics, label **End A as Home end** and **End B as Away end**. Do not invent other end names; keep snake_case `end_a`/`end_b` on the wire.
Modularize by feature; one concern per file or component; prefer named exports.
Style each component explicitly rather than relying on inherited or contextual styles.
}

NamingConstraints {
Use clear, descriptive, consistent naming.
Components should be postfixed with `Component`.
Props should be the component's name, postfixed with `ComponentProps`.
File names: kebab-case. e.g. `user-avatar-component.tsx`, `use-auth-session.ts`.
Zustand stores: `*-store.ts` exporting `use*Store`. e.g. `app-store.ts` → `useAppStore`.
TanStack Query hooks: `use-*-query.ts` / `use-*-mutation.ts`. e.g. `use-sessions-query.ts`, `use-create-session-mutation.ts`.
Platform-specific files use the `.ios.tsx` / `.android.tsx` / `.native.tsx` suffix convention rather than embedded `Platform.OS` conditionals, when the divergence is significant.
}

TypeConstraints {
Use proper React Native TypeScript types: GestureResponderEvent (onPress/onLongPress), NativeSyntheticEvent<TextInputChangeEventData> (TextInput onChange), NativeSyntheticEvent<TextInputKeyPressEventData>, ReactNode, React.Ref<T>, ComponentProps<typeof View>, ComponentProps<typeof SomeComponent>. Never use generic () => void or (event: any) => void.
When extending RN primitives or existing components, use ComponentProps to inherit their props: ComponentProps<typeof TextInput>, ComponentProps<typeof Pressable>, ComponentProps<typeof ExistingComponent>.
}
